---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { about, principles } from '../data/product';
// Copy from the original lockstep.uk site. Founder story written by Andrew.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Lockstep is designed for people who want to stay in control of gambling without being told what that control must look like."
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="About Lockstep" title="What is Lockstep">
    {about.paragraphs.map((text) => <p>{text}</p>)}
  </PageHero>

  <section class="section section--surface" id="philosophy" aria-labelledby="principles-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="stack reveal principles-head">
        <h2 id="principles-heading">Philosophy &amp; principles</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Lockstep is built around a small set of principles that guide every design decision.
          They keep us focused on what matters most: real support, real progress, and real choice.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="principles">
        {principles.map((item, i) => (
          <li class="principle reveal">
            <span class="principle__num" aria-hidden="true">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="principle__text">{item.text}</p>
            <p>{item.detail}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="founder-heading">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 id="founder-heading">Meet the founder</h2>
        <p><strong>Andrew Brink</strong>, Founder</p>
        <p>
          Like many students, I started gambling casually at university. It began with the
          occasional sports bet among friends or a late trip to the casino after a night out, but
          over time I noticed it was taking up more of my money, time and headspace than I
          wanted. When I went looking for something to help me keep it in check, all I could find
          was reactive support designed for people already in crisis. It took a one-size-fits-all
          approach and asked for a commitment I wasn't ready to make: to see myself as someone in
          crisis and to never gamble again.
        </p>
        <p>
          At 19, I attended a virtual Gamblers Anonymous meeting and left feeling more out of
          place than when I arrived. The stories I heard were worlds away from my own; many of
          the people there had spent decades in recovery, and their experiences bore little
          resemblance to the app-based gambling I knew. Next to what they had been through,
          saying I had a gambling problem after losing £200 felt almost dishonest, and being told
          that the only answer was to stop altogether felt like an enormous leap. What I needed
          wasn't a dramatic intervention but something relevant, private and practical, along
          with people in similar circumstances I could talk to.
        </p>
        <p>
          Lockstep is the support I wish I'd had back then: free, private and judgement-free,
          meeting you wherever you are. Rather than prescribing a single path, it lets you decide
          what control looks like for you, offering practical tools, genuine alternatives and a
          community of people who understand what you're going through. Wherever you are with
          gambling, you don't have to figure it out on your own.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .principles-head {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .principles {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .principles {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-lg) var(--space-xl);
    }
  }

  .principle {
    max-width: none;
    padding-top: var(--space-sm);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--color-green);
  }

  .principle__num {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
    color: var(--color-emerald);
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .principle p {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .principle__text {
    color: var(--color-green);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
